The GRUB boot menu theme in usr/share/grub/themes/amethystora follows the
gfxmenu theme layout of grub2-themes by Vince Liuice, licensed under the GNU
General Public License, version 3:

  - grub2-themes  https://github.com/vinceliuice/grub2-themes

Its artwork is Amethystora's own, generated by branding/generate.mjs; no files
from that project are included.

The icon theme in usr/share/icons/candy-icons is candy-icons by Eliver Lara,
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3:

  - candy-icons  https://github.com/EliverLara/candy-icons

It is not the theme as its author publishes it. Amethystora has modified it
since September 2026, and makes the changes again each time an image is built:
build_files/base/10-icons.sh installs it from upstream, changes the theme's
inheritance, drops the symbolic names outside places/, removes the icons that
redraw another maker's logo, adds aliases for the applications this image
ships, and adds the icons kept in build_files/shared/candy-icons, drawn for
Amethystora in the theme's style. The licence ships with it in
usr/share/licenses/candy-icons. The icons added are:

  - amethystora-security-status.svg, whose shield is the theme's own, from its
    preferences-system-privacy.svg. It is a modified part of candy-icons and
    is licensed, like the theme, under the GNU General Public License, version
    3, not under the Apache License. So are its two copies: the one in
    usr/share/icons/hicolor, and the one drawn in the window of Amethystora
    Security (usr/lib/amethystora-security/resources/app/index.html).
  - io.github.kolunmi.Bazaar.svg, drawn for Amethystora in the theme's style
    after Bazaar's own icon, a market stall under an awning.
  - amethystora-notes.svg and amethystora-backups.svg, which are Amethystora's
    own drawings.

Of the application icons, the theme as Amethystora ships it keeps the
pictograms of a job, such as a calculator or an envelope, and four logos in
the theme's style: Bazaar's, drawn here, and Flatseal's, Mission Center's and
VSCodium's, drawn by the theme. Their makers publish no trademark terms for
them. An application whose logo the theme redrew shows the icon its maker
gave it instead. The names and logos of the applications in an image are
trademarks of their owners, who do not sponsor or endorse Amethystora.

